Z||000000||Voyd||12-26-1999||01:06 AM||||anyone tried this thing? id like to know about my cars history as it was pretty beaten up when i got it. but i dont wanna get ripped off either.<P>thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||WisconsinGT||12-26-1999||01:33 AM||||I used it before buying my 88GT. I ran several vehicals through CarFax. I would recomend it. It will give you a piece of mind about the car you are buying. Good luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||12-26-1999||10:37 AM||||Its a good service.  I used it when shopping for my Jeep.  If you the vehicle comes from a state where regular inspections are required then you are likely to get lots of info, otherwise you'll just see a title history and maybe some dealer service records.<P>All in all worth the $20.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||12-26-1999||10:58 AM||||I was disappointed in the results of the carfax report for my 85 se, it only went back two years and really did not tell much. But, they have a satisfaction guarantee so if you're not happy with the report you can get a refund. I dont put a lot of faith in their reports either because as a joke I ran my wife's car that was bought new by her parents and it had 4 title history entries, but my car that has been totaled in another state and transfered twice since then only had 2 title history entries. They will not tell you if their info is complete or not, so it is still buyer beware.||||reg||1
